  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A$ be the centre of the circle $x^{2}+y^{2}-2 x-4 y-20=0 .$ Let $B(1,7)$ and\r\n$D(4,-2)$ be two points on the circle such that tangents at $B$ and $D$ meet at $C$. The area of the quadrilateral $A B C D$ is",
    "image": null
  },
